diff --git a/readme.md b/readme.md
index 467d746..30b5fd5 100644
--- a/readme.md
+++ b/readme.md
@@ -90,7 +90,21 @@ The `context` object contains:
 - `attemptNumber` - The attempt number (starts at 1)
 - `retriesLeft` - Number of retries remaining
 - `retriesConsumed` - Number of retries consumed so far
-- `retryDelay` - The delay in milliseconds before the next retry (based on `minTimeout`, `factor`, `maxTimeout`, and `randomize`). The actual delay may be shorter if it would exceed `maxRetryTime`. This is `0` when no retry will occur based on the checks completed before the current callback runs. `shouldConsumeRetry` is the exception: it is shown the delay that would be used, since deciding whether to consume the retry is what it is being asked.
+- `retryDelay` - The delay in milliseconds before the next retry (based on `minTimeout`, `factor`, `maxTimeout`, and `randomize`, or the error's `retryAfter` if that is longer). The actual delay may be shorter if it would exceed `maxRetryTime`. This is `0` when no retry will occur based on the checks completed before the current callback runs. `shouldConsumeRetry` is the exception: it is shown the delay that would be used, since deciding whether to consume the retry is what it is being asked.
+- `elapsedTime` - Milliseconds since `pRetry` was called, measured when the context is created
+
+### Retry-After
+
+If the error an attempt throws has a numeric `retryAfter` (in seconds), the next attempt waits at least that long. It is a floor: the usual backoff is used if it is longer. It is not limited by `maxTimeout`, but `maxRetryTime` still applies. A `retryAfter` that is not a finite, non-negative number is ignored.
+
+```js
+class RateLimitError extends Error {
+	constructor(retryAfter) {
+		super('Too many requests');
+		this.retryAfter = retryAfter;
+	}
+}
+```
 
 The `onFailedAttempt` function can return a promise. For example, to add a [delay](https://github.com/sindresorhus/delay):
 
